(2132185, 288299, 5885, '<td valign="top">Hail, this was a good shot technically. Lighting,color, focus were all there. However, I feel you got a lot of low votes, because it does feel romantic. Perhaps a single rose (a flower more commonly associated with romance)? Nonetheless, don''t give up... it can only get better. <br/> <br/>Think about the challenge when you shoot. Here''s what I''ve learned: If you go too far outside the box with your subject a good deal of voters will shoot you down. I''m often the victim of this, but socres don''t matter to me as much as putting the shot out there.<br/> <br/>On the opposite side of the coin, if your shot is too mundane, it will also be shot down. DPC is about pleasing a mass audience. To ribbon, you need a technically good shot with lots of mass appeal. By mass appeal, I mean, it has to be something most voters can associate with the challenge.<br/> <br/>Anyway, I hope this helps and I look forward to seeing more work from you.<br/> <br/></td>', 'Hail, this was a good shot technically. Lighting,color, focus were all there. However, I feel you got a lot of low votes, because it does feel romantic. Perhaps a single rose (a flower more commonly associated with romance)? Nonetheless, don''t give up... it can only get better.  Think about the challenge when you shoot. Here''s what I''ve learned: If you go too far outside the box with your subject a good deal of voters will shoot you down. I''m often the victim of this, but socres don''t matter to me as much as putting the shot out there. On the opposite side of the coin, if your shot is too mundane, it will also be shot down. DPC is about pleasing a mass audience. To ribbon, you need a technically good shot with lots of mass appeal. By mass appeal, I mean, it has to be something most voters can associate with the challenge. Anyway, I hope this helps and I look forward to seeing more work from you. ', '2006-02-08 01:37:33.000000', NULL, 0),
